  "description": "＊From April 13 - May12, 2024, \"Japanese Art and Design: The Irises Screens, National Treasure\" is ON. Please visit our website for online booking. Entry to the garden requires museum entrance fee. - Thanks to a bequest from Nezu Kaichiro (1860-1940), the collection of more than 7,600 Japanese and East Asian works of pre-modern art forms the basis of seven exbitions in an year, each of which focuses on a different theme: painting, calligraphy, ceramics, lacquerwre, textiles and metalworks. Online timed-entry reservation is recommended. For the exhibition schedule and reservation, please visit the museum' website.",
